WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.553
An AI coding assistant does not automatically know the history, architecture, or conventions of a project.

2
00:00:06.553 --> 00:00:13.515
A short feature request may be enough for a toy example, but real repositories have existing interfaces,

3
00:00:13.515 --> 00:00:17.201
naming patterns, data models, tests, build commands, and tradeoffs.

4
00:00:17.201 --> 00:00:24.164
If the assistant cannot see the facts that govern the change, it will fill gaps with guesses.

5
00:00:24.164 --> 00:00:30.307
Useful context includes the files directly involved in the change, nearby tests, interface definitions, schemas,

6
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:33.584
dependency versions, error messages, and the runtime environment.

7
00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:36.860
It also includes behavior that must remain unchanged.

8
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:44.232
If you are adding a feature to an existing settings page, the assistant should see the current component,

9
00:00:44.232 --> 00:00:48.738
the service it calls, and the tests that describe current behavior.

10
00:00:48.738 --> 00:00:55.700
Without that grounding, the answer may be locally reasonable but inconsistent with the rest of the application.

11
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.567
More context is not always better context.

12
00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:04.301
Pasting an entire repository without direction can bury the important details under unrelated material.

13
00:01:04.301 --> 00:01:08.806
Good context is selected because it affects the decision at hand.

14
00:01:08.806 --> 00:01:16.178
A current type definition, migration file, test suite, or project README is usually more authoritative than an old

15
00:01:16.178 --> 00:01:19.864
comment or a confident guess made by the model.

16
00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:22.321
Context can also contain untrusted instructions.

17
00:01:22.321 --> 00:01:30.513
A log file, issue description, web page, or dependency document may include text that looks like a command to the

18
00:01:30.513 --> 00:01:30.922
assistant.

19
00:01:30.922 --> 00:01:35.427
Treat that material as project data unless you intentionally decide otherwise.

20
00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:42.390
The model should use it to understand the problem, not automatically follow every embedded instruction it encounters.

21
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.847
Supplying context is an iterative skill.

22
00:01:44.847 --> 00:01:48.533
Start with the goal and the most relevant files.

23
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:54.267
If the assistant identifies a dependency, or a failing test reveals an incorrect assumption,

24
00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:56.724
add the next piece of evidence.

25
00:01:56.724 --> 00:02:00.001
The aim is not to overwhelm the model.

26
00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:08.192
The aim is to give it enough reliable project truth to make a small, coherent change that fits the codebase.
